336	GUY	GGXWDG	Guyana	General government gross debt	"Gross debt consists of all liabilities that require payment or payments of interest and/or principal by the debtor to the creditor at a date or dates in the future. This includes debt liabilities in the form of SDRs, currency and deposits, debt securities, loans, insurance, pensions and standardized guarantee schemes, and other accounts payable. Thus, all liabilities in the GFSM 2001 system are debt, except for equity and investment fund shares and financial derivatives and employee stock options. Debt can be valued at current market, nominal, or face values (GFSM 2001, paragraph 7.110)."	National currency	Billions	"Source: Ministry of Finance or Treasury Latest actual data: 2023 Fiscal assumptions: Consistent with other sectors. Reporting in calendar year: Yes Start/end months of reporting year: January/December GFS Manual used: Government Finance Statistics Manual (GFSM) 1986 Basis of recording: Cash General government includes: Central Government; Social Security Funds; Nonfinancial Public Corporation; Valuation of public debt: Nominal value Instruments included in gross and net debt: Currency and Deposits;. Net debt is equal to gross debt minus CG deposits in the banking system. In 2016, CG was borrowing from the CB, therefore, CG had no deposit and the net debt is equal to gross debt. Primary domestic currency: Guyanese dollar Data last updated: 09/2024"	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	228.956	243.993	257.182	265.492	294.796	311.599	295.141	301.467	310.476	283.138	211.459	241.397	273.733	309.031	347.609	367.812	351.441	326.24	369.647	405.855	420.57	467.729	469.915	582.721	690.255	803.724	939.592	"1,223.14"	"1,327.34"	"1,443.70"	"1,514.61"	"1,539.96"	"1,566.69"	2023
